srow(305, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE LORD SAID TO MOSES: TAKE JOSHUA SON OF NUN" (Numbers 27:18) — TAKE A STRONG MAN LIKE YOURSELF; "TAKE" IS ONLY BY TAKING, FOR A COMPANION IS ACQUIRED ONLY WITH GREAT DIFFICULTY — HENCE THEY SAID: A MAN ACQUIRES A COMPANION TO READ WITH HIM, REPEAT WITH HIM, EAT AND DRINK WITH HIM AND REVEAL HIS SECRETS TO HIM ("TWO ARE BETTER THAN ONE", "THE THREEFOLD CORD IS NOT QUICKLY BROKEN", Ecclesiastes 4:9, 12). THE HOLY ONE ANSWERS MOSES: GIVE JOSHUA AN INTERPRETER, THAT HE ASK AND EXPOUND AND TEACH RULINGS IN YOUR LIFETIME, LEST ISRAEL SAY TO HIM: IN YOUR MASTER\'S LIFE YOU DID NOT SPEAK, AND NOW YOU SPEAK? SOME SAY: HE RAISED HIM FROM THE GROUND AND SAT HIM BETWEEN HIS KNEES, AND MOSES AND ISRAEL LIFTED THEIR HEADS TO HEAR JOSHUA\'S WORDS — BLESSED BE THE LORD WHO GAVE TORAH TO ISRAEL BY THE HAND OF MOSES OUR MASTER. The HEADLESS piska\'s first row ({SP_(305, 1, "קח", "לך", "גברתן", "כמותך")} "take a strong man like yourself"; {SP_(305, 1, "תן", "לו", "תורגמן", "ליהושע")} "give Joshua an interpreter"; {SP_(305, 1, "ומורה", "הוריות", "בחייך")} "and teaching rulings in your lifetime"): THE COMMISSION\'S CONTENT — Joshua to teach WHILE MOSES LIVES (the compile: the office\'s status begins at the Tent, before the death — its install the chapter\'s own day, not 34:5\'s); the study companion (Avot 1:6 the translator\'s parallel — the testing shelf). The Writings\' seat cited (Ecclesiastes 4:9, 12), never read. Fresh.')
